    "title": "Boy rushed to hospital after being hit by a car in Brisbane",
    "text": "By Zak Wheeler for Daily Mail Australia\nPublished: 21:48 GMT, February 13, 2025 | Updated: 21:55 GMT, February 13, 2025\nA child was urgently transferred to the hospital with serious injuries after he was hit by a car.\nThe child, under 16, was beaten in the corner of Wadeville and Kent streets in Heathwood, 21 km south of Brisbane’s CBD, at 7.35 am on Thursday.\nMultiple paramedic teams attended the scene.\nThe child suffered serious head wounds, abdominal and hip.\nHe was urgently taken to the Queensland Children’s Hospital in a stable condition.\nA child has been urgently taken to the Queensland Children’s Hospital (in the photo) as a stable condition after he was hit by a car in South Brisbane on Thursday morning.\nShare or comment on this article: the child hastened to the hospital after being hit by a car in Brisbane\n(Tagstotranslate) Dailymail (T) News (T) Brisbane",
